      {
        "id": 55315,
        "name": "Chaosmancer",
        "username": "Chaosmancer",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/chaosmancer/{size}/1977_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-03-21T04:09:45.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Couple of cool things I noticed about Mr. Fixer in my game against Spite.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Toolbox is equipment, so Spite can bounce that back... and it was returning to your hand anyways. I was playing Expatriette, Wraith, and Fixer and that bouncing drug was the first card out. Stuff like the Toolbox was a blessing, plus the math worked out to where I only needed to bounce one card every round.</p><p>If you have the hoist chain out and use either charge or overdrive you double the -1 damage. This, Stun Bolt, and Expattriete using Nitrogen rounds and speed loading let me lock down Spite for multiple rounds when I was really low on health.</p><p>This would have been an amazing fight if I hadn't realized later I had forgotten Spite's play phase due to his end of turn effect. Playing solo is still a challenge for me and it was late</p>",
        "post_number": 25,
        "post_type": 1,
