      {
        "id": 55318,
        "name": "TheSoundOfTrees",
        "username": "TheSoundOfTrees",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/t/da6949/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-03-21T10:19:30.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"flamethrower49\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/f/838e76/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> flamethrower49:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I'm curious how people use Fixer against Spite. &nbsp;What combo do you go for? &nbsp;Bouncing Toolbox aside, does he pull his weight in this fight, in your opinion?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>He is a very good hero against Spite (on normal, I still did not try Spite on advanced).</p>\n<p>The style that makes all damage dealt to spite irreducible if you can damage him + bloody knuckle is great, it makes the protection drug irrelevant - and bloody knuckle gets back to your hand. If you can have the pipe too, you have a tanking Mr Fixer who can break Spite's protection each turn. Or with hoist chain, you break spite's defenses and attack power…</p>\n<p>If you can't manage this, Irreducible damage + hoist chain is a good alternative.</p>\n<p>Thanks to toolbox, you can have a lot of cards in hand, very useful to save some of the victims, especially because fixer doesn't need a lot of cards.</p>\n<p>The drug that have you take a card back in hand allows Mr Fixer to get his Styles back in hand - so he gets a lot of freedom. Not always useful, but it can be.</p>\n<p>Compound XI (toxic damage any time you use a power) can also turn into a curse for Spite, with Fixer's Driving Mantis. Redirect the damage - maybe twice thanks to Overdrive ! You can even do it after Spite has his damage bonus if someone can hoist chain/stun bolt him.</p>\n<p>My easier games against Spite have been with Mr Fixer - Wraith is good against him, too, but more fragile. Combine the two heroes and it works really well. Smoke Bombing coumpound XI damage to Mr Fixer, who then redirects it, is always fun. Add Ra and his \"returning each and every turn\" Staff and Legacy just because, and Spite will suffer.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 28,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:30:00.570Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
