      {
        "id": 55323,
        "name": "Reckless",
        "username": "Reckless",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/reckless/{size}/2467_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-03-21T18:35:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Spite is Mister Fixer's best friend.&nbsp; With his Drug that mills five cards off of your deck, Spite effectively weaponizes Scrapyard to get you exactly what Tool you need, and the Drug that bounces cards makes Toolbox and Bloody Knuckles the coolest cards in existence.&nbsp; On top of that, nearly all of Fixer's Styles and Tools apply to Spite by either upping his damage, dealing Irreducible damage, or redirecting Spite's smaller damage effects (which he will heal if on his first side, but still...it's a pretty good temporary DR of 1-2).&nbsp; Also, Pipe Wrench provides DR and damage, Hoist Chain reduces Spite's Damage, Dual Crowbars increases damage and can potentially smack down any pesky Environment targets as a secondary effect, Tire Iron is...a card, and Jack Handle is still totally awesome even if it isn't that impressive against Spite.&nbsp; I still find Riveting Crane to be completely disappointing, as it cannot be used on it's own against the lowest DR of 1.<br><br>The point is, Mister Fixer is Spite's worst nightmare.</p>",
        "post_number": 33,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:30:00.962Z",
