      {
        "id": 55324,
        "name": "flamethrower49",
        "username": "flamethrower49",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/f/838e76/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-03-21T20:01:30.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>So... let's talk about Bloody Knuckles vs. Spite.&nbsp; It's nice that you can bounce it before Spite does three instances of damage to you, and we'll assume we're fighting in the harmless kitten environment.&nbsp; But whenever I've tried it, it always results in 5 damage to Fixer when Fixer tries to use his power, or 4 if he thought to bring his Pipe Wrench.&nbsp; This seems untenable.&nbsp; If he forces through Riveting Crane with this, then you label him a hero, but if he doesn't, it doesn't seem like this works all that well.</p><p>I'm just trying to understand.</p>",
        "post_number": 34,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:30:01.038Z",
