      {
        "id": 55325,
        "name": "Reckless",
        "username": "Reckless",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/reckless/{size}/2467_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-03-21T20:19:42.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I suppose that's true.&nbsp; My group just finds Spite to be pretty adorable when he's just bouncing cards and dealing damage on his flipped side.&nbsp; We generally don't mind it that Spite deals harsh damage when he can so easily have his damage reduced, prevented, or redirected.&nbsp; Worst case scenario is that he whittles the team down a little and then we completely tear him apart.&nbsp; I definitely see your point, though.&nbsp; That revenge damage can really smart after a few rounds.</p>",
